{
	"$comment": "The Python/TS contract for client-portal customisation. apps/api/tests/test_branding.py and the pkgs/ui registry test BOTH assert against this file, so the two sides cannot drift silently. Settings keys are snake_case because they ride the wire exactly as pydantic dumps them. `variants` are the DATA shapes a block can take; `looks` are its VISUAL designs (per-instance `look` setting; 'auto' follows the portal finish — card finish ⇒ 'card', ledger finish ⇒ the type's chrome-less look). portfolioHeader carries no looks: its variants ARE its looks. Change this file only together with both sides.",
	"$comment_defaultPages": "A `defaultPages` entry's `blocks` IS the page's `default` audience layout; the optional `individual`/`organisation` arrays are audience overrides in the same block shape (absent ⇒ that audience follows `blocks`, which is why the pre-audience entries below need no rewrite). A block's `id` is optional and defaults to its type name — spell it out only where a page holds two blocks of one type, and keep the id of the block that also exists in `blocks` so an override reads as the copy-on-write of the default it is. `settings` objects are MINIMAL (an entry with none is omitted): both sides validate them through the type's settings model before comparing, so the canonical dump's untouched defaults must not be written out here.",
	"blocks": {
		"portfolioHeader": {
			"variants": ["auto", "hero", "canvas", "ledger", "compact"],
			"settings": ["variant", "show_chart", "actions", "default_period"]
		},
		"accounts": {
			"variants": ["auto", "stack", "cards", "table", "summary"],
